course: dictionary
lesson: 14328
title: Obsessed: more than just liking
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Obsessed is a strong word. It means your mind keeps going back to one thing, again and again. Context shows you how strong the feeling is. «Mia is obsessed with dinosaurs» means she thinks about them all the time and talks about them even when nobody asks.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Sam is obsessed with football» tells you he loves football, but «Sam cannot stop thinking about the penalty he missed, even at night» shows the feeling is so big that it fills his mind. Ask yourself: is this just a lot of liking, or are thoughts taking over?
explain: Obsessed can also be a health word. Some people have thoughts that keep coming back and are very hard to stop. This can be part of an illness called OCD (obsessive-compulsive disorder). That is not the same as liking things tidy. If you meet obsessed in a health text, ask a grown-up or check a dictionary.
fact: Obsessed is an adjective, and its verb is obsess: obsess, obsesses, obsessed, obsessing.
fact: «Obsessed with» means you love something or think about it all the time, as in «obsessed with dinosaurs».
fact: Informal use: «I'm obsessed with this song» means you love it very much, and it is fine to say so.
fact: Health use: obsessive thoughts keep coming back and are hard to stop. OCD is an illness, not just a liking for neat things.
fact: A quick check: swap in «thinking about it all the time». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
exercise: «Ava is obsessed with horses; she draws them, reads about them and dreams about them.» What does obsessed mean here? | *Thinking about horses all the time | Afraid of horses | Bored of horses | Riding horses slowly
exercise: «Ben was obsessed by the video game and forgot his dinner.» Which clue shows how strong the feeling was? | *forgot his dinner | Ben was | obsessed by | video game
exercise: Which word is the base verb form of obsessed? | obsessive | *obsess | obsessions | obsession
test: «Lily is obsessed with cats: she has posters, toys and three books about them.» What does obsessed mean? | Only slightly interested | *Loving or thinking about something all the time | Tired of something | Scared of something
test: In a health text, «obsessive thoughts keep coming back and are hard to stop.» What does this show? | A happy memory | *A thought that keeps returning and is hard to switch off | Liking things to be tidy | Something that is fun to do
exam: Which sentence uses obsessed in the health sense? | Tom is obsessed with his new bike | Grandma is obsessed with her garden | *Her worrying thoughts keep returning, and she finds them very hard to stop | Our class is obsessed with the school play
